# static-analysis.sh baseline: findings triaged as false positives, or as
# what a tool cannot see past. The gate fails on a finding not listed
# here and on an entry listed without a reason.
# One line per finding (repeated when reported more than once):
# tool<TAB>file<TAB>check<TAB>message, digits as N, no line numbers.
# A "## <reason>" line documents the entries below it.
# Regenerate with static-analysis.sh -u (reasons of findings still
# reported are kept).

## CloseAllApps() walks app_list_, which only ever holds the non-null apps OnLaunchUrl() and CreateWindowForAppPage() add; the analyzer assumes an element may be NULL.
gcc-O0	src/core/web_app_manager.cc	-Wanalyzer-null-argument	use of NULL ‘app’ where non-null expected [CWE-N]

## WAM is built with -fno-exceptions, so gcc -fanalyzer assumes operator new may return NULL. libc++'s operator new does not return NULL: when it cannot allocate it throws std::bad_alloc, which nothing in WAM catches, so the process ends. The NULL followed here (and the vector storage that comes from it) cannot occur.
gcc-O0	src/core/web_app_factory_manager_impl.cc	-Wanalyzer-possible-null-argument	use of possibly-NULL ‘operator new(N)’ where non-null expected [CWE-N]
gcc-O0	src/core/web_app_factory_manager_impl.cc	-Wanalyzer-possible-null-argument	use of possibly-NULL ‘operator new(N)’ where non-null expected [CWE-N]
gcc-O0	src/core/web_app_manager.cc	-Wanalyzer-possible-null-argument	use of possibly-NULL ‘operator new(N)’ where non-null expected [CWE-N]
gcc-O0	src/platform/web_app_wayland.h	-Wanalyzer-possible-null-dereference	dereference of possibly-NULL ‘operator new(N)’ [CWE-N]
gcc-O0	src/plugin/web_app_factory_luna.cc	-Wanalyzer-possible-null-argument	use of possibly-NULL ‘operator new(N)’ where non-null expected [CWE-N]
gcc-O0	src/plugin/web_app_factory_luna.cc	-Wanalyzer-possible-null-argument	use of possibly-NULL ‘operator new(N)’ where non-null expected [CWE-N]
